## Anti-Patterns to Avoid

```typescript
// ❌ Don't test implementation details
expect(component.state.isOpen).toBe(true)
expect(wrapper.instance().handleClick).toBeDefined()

// ✅ Test behavior
expect(screen.getByRole('dialog')).toBeVisible()

// ❌ Don't use container queries
const { container } = render(<Component />)
container.querySelector('.my-class')

// ✅ Use accessible queries
screen.getByRole('button', { name: /submit/i })

// ❌ Don't test third-party libraries
expect(axios.get).toHaveBeenCalled()

// ✅ Test your code's behavior with mocked dependencies
expect(screen.getByText(/user data/i)).toBeInTheDocument()

// ❌ Don't snapshot everything
expect(component).toMatchSnapshot()

// ✅ Snapshot only stable, visual components
expect(screen.getByRole('button')).toMatchSnapshot()

// ❌ Don't use arbitrary waits
await new Promise(r => setTimeout(r, 1000))

// ✅ Use waitFor or findBy queries
await waitFor(() => expect(screen.getByText(/loaded/i)).toBeInTheDocument())
await screen.findByText(/loaded/i)

// ❌ Don't forget to clean up
// (Vitest/RTL handles this, but watch for manual subscriptions)

// ✅ Use afterEach for manual cleanup
afterEach(() => {
  vi.clearAllMocks()
})
```

## Coverage Guidelines

- Aim for 80%+ coverage on critical paths (auth, data mutations)
- Don't chase 100% - some code isn't worth testing
- Focus on:
  - User interactions
  - Edge cases
  - Error handling
  - Async operations
